"""Direct question-design review of Sanskrit learning and sacred geography."""
from review_angle_plans import revise_domain, audit

SANSKRIT = """history_origins|A Sanskrit Teaching Method's History|When did one named approach to teaching Sanskrit enter use?|Compare dated textbooks, syllabi, and teacher accounts.
famous_examples|A Successful Course Examined|What can one often praised Sanskrit course actually teach beginners to do?|Inspect curriculum, learner baseline, assessment, and outcomes.
hidden_stories|Teachers and Learners Behind a Program|Whose work is missing from a course success story?|Use consented student and teacher accounts with institutional data.
beginner_explainers|A First Sanskrit Learning Goal|What can a beginner reasonably read or say after one course level?|Define script, grammar, vocabulary, and assessment rather than promising fluency.
advanced_concepts|Reading Across Registers|How does a learner move from textbook Sanskrit to a specified text type?|Compare forms, vocabulary, commentary, and prerequisites.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Why Learners Stall|Which part of a course causes a measured learning bottleneck?|Use assessment errors, interviews, and alternative explanations.
technology_innovation|A Digital Sanskrit Tool Tested|Does one app improve reading or listening accuracy?|Compare benchmark tasks, source quality, accessibility, and feedback.
people_personalities|A Teacher's Pedagogical Contribution|What did one named educator change in Sanskrit instruction?|Read their materials and documented learner use.
major_events|A Curriculum Revision|What changed after one dated syllabus reform?|Compare objectives, resources, teacher training, and results.
how_it_works|From Script to Sentence|Which skills must a learner combine to understand one short passage?|Map script recognition, word division, morphology, and context.
rise_fall|A Program's Enrollment Over Time|Why did participation grow or decline?|Check admission rules, staffing, demand, and counting definitions.
then_vs_now|Two Sanskrit Classrooms|How did learning goals and materials change across two periods?|Compare equivalent course levels and assessment methods.
future_developments|A Better Learning Pathway|What would a proposed course change need to improve?|Specify learner group, prerequisites, teaching capacity, and measure.
myths_vs_facts|An Easy-Fluency Claim|Does a claim about rapid mastery match assessed learner performance?|Define fluency and evaluate comparable learners over time.
documentary_stories|One Learner's Reading Journey|How did a consented learner work through a particular text?|Pair account with tasks, corrections, and course context.
text_source|Choosing a Teachable Passage|Which edition and register make one passage suitable for a course level?|Check provenance, script, vocabulary, and commentary.
interpretive_lineages|Two Ways to Parse a Verse|How do teachers explain one grammatical ambiguity?|Compare syntax, commentary, and instructional goal.
lived_practice|Sanskrit Beyond the Classroom|Where does one learner encounter Sanskrit in community life?|Use consented accounts without assuming a religious use for all learners.
ritual_sequence|Learning Language for an Observance|Which linguistic skills help understand a named public recitation?|Explain comprehension goals without prescribing ritual performance.
language_translation|A Translation Exercise's Limits|What does a literal translation miss in a selected passage?|Compare grammar, idiom, genre, and context.
regional_variants|Teaching Sanskrit in Two Settings|How do two programs differ in language of instruction and access?|Match learner level, resources, and goals.
art_and_devotion|Reading a Verse in Art|How can a learner connect a Sanskrit inscription or poem to an artwork?|Use provenance, text, translation, and artist context.
community_memory|A School's Teaching Tradition|How do alumni and records describe a program's history?|Compare memory, syllabi, enrollment, and institutional change.
ethics_in_context|Who Can Access the Classroom?|Which fees, language choices, disability barriers, or entry rules shape access?|Use institutional policy and affected learner voices.
source_and_history|A Textbook's Source Passage|How accurately does a teaching edition reproduce its cited source?|Compare source edition, omitted context, and editorial changes.
encounter_and_exchange|Sanskrit Learning Across Communities|How do learners with different aims use the same course?|Compare academic, artistic, and devotional goals with consent.
contemporary_voice|A Learner and Teacher Assess Progress|Where do their views of difficulty or achievement differ?|Use named tasks and consented accounts.
field_textual_lineage|A Verse Across Editions|Which variant matters for a learner's reading?|Compare witnesses and editorial notes at an appropriate level.
field_regional_practice|One Local Sanskrit Program|How is a course taught and assessed in a named place?|Document curriculum, teacher preparation, and learner access.
field_translation_choice|Two Renderings of a Sentence|Which grammatical evidence supports each rendering?|Show word division, inflection, syntax, and genre.
field_ritual_context|Understanding a Public Chant|How does language study change comprehension for one learner group?|Ask participants; distinguish meaning from ritual authority.
field_community_interpretation|A Community Teaches a Text|How do local teachers explain one contested line?|Attribute their interpretation and present alternatives."""

SACRED = """history_origins|A Sacred Landscape in Dated Sources|When do named places and their associations appear in the record?|Compare texts, maps, archaeology, and later community memory.
famous_examples|A Known Sacred Landscape in Context|How do distinct communities understand one well-known place?|Attribute each account and trace dated stewardship.
hidden_stories|Custodians of a Sacred Place|Whose care work or knowledge is missing from a visitor map?|Use consented local voices and institutional records.
beginner_explainers|What Makes a Place Sacred?|How does one community define the relationship among land, story, and practice?|Represent its own terms rather than assigning sacredness from outside.
advanced_concepts|Overlapping Sacred Geographies|How do two communities map meaning onto the same landscape?|Compare place names, access protocols, history, and coexistence.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|A Disputed Site Identification|Which evidence supports competing locations for one historical place?|Separate textual description, archaeology, maps, and living tradition.
technology_innovation|Mapping a Sensitive Site|Can a digital map help stewardship without exposing restricted locations?|Ask custodians about consent, precision, access, and data control.
people_personalities|A Landscape's Documented Steward|What did one named custodian or organizer do for a place?|Use records and community perspectives beyond a heroic account.
major_events|A Sacred Place Changes Access|What happened after one dated law, road, or conservation decision?|Compare access, ritual use, ecology, and local livelihoods.
how_it_works|A Place Network, Not One Point|How do named sites, routes, and seasonal practices connect?|Map community descriptions and distinguish public from restricted knowledge.
rise_fall|Changing Use of a Sacred Area|Why did visits or observances increase or decline?|Compare counting methods, policy, mobility, and community choices.
then_vs_now|One Landscape Across Generations|What changed in names, access, ecology, and stewardship?|Pair dated maps with consented living accounts.
future_developments|A Land-Use Proposal at a Sacred Site|What would one proposal need to protect community access and ecology?|Compare plans, rights, impact assessment, and custodial priorities.
myths_vs_facts|A Map as Proof of Sacred History?|Does one popular map accurately represent sources and community knowledge?|Check date, scale, naming, uncertainty, and permissions.
documentary_stories|A Sacred Place Through Records and Voices|What do maps, legal files, and custodial accounts reveal?|Explain gaps and attribute sacred meanings.
map_vs_ground|Mapped Boundary and Lived Place|Where does an official map diverge from community place knowledge?|Compare scale, language, access, and field evidence with consent.
route_choices|Different Paths to Meaningful Sites|Why do community members use different routes or sequences?|Ask practitioners and respect restricted paths.
seasonality|A Sacred Calendar and the Land|How do season and ecology shape one public observance?|Compare calendars, environmental data, and local interpretation.
local_voice|Residents and Custodians Speak|How do nearby people describe benefits, burdens, and obligations?|Use diverse consented accounts without assuming one community voice.
landscape_process|Physical Change at a Sacred Site|How has erosion, water, vegetation, or development changed one place?|Use dated environmental records and attributed cultural meaning.
accessibility|Who Can Reach or Use the Place?|Which mobility, cost, law, or language barriers affect a defined group?|Compare rules and facilities with affected voices.
infrastructure|Services Around a Sacred Landscape|Which transport, sanitation, or conservation service is under pressure?|Use capacity and usage data with local priorities.
environmental_pressure|Land Use and Sacred Ecology|Which measurable pressure affects one landscape?|Separate visitor impact from other causes and respect local stewardship.
safety_decision|A Site-Access Decision|What evidence shaped one public access or crowd policy?|Read official plans and community input; avoid real-time route guidance.
place_history|Layers of a Named Place|How did a sacred site and surrounding settlement change together?|Use dated land, building, and oral-history evidence.
comparison_of_places|Two Sacred Landscapes, Different Rules|How do two sites manage comparable access pressures?|Match scale, legal context, community authority, and ecology.
responsible_access|Who Decides What Can Be Shared?|How do custodians set visitor and researcher boundaries?|Use current protocols and consent, omitting restricted detail.
field_source_tradition|Place Names Across Sources|Which textual and oral witnesses name one site?|Compare language, date, provenance, and uncertainty.
field_lived_practice|A Living Landscape Practice|How does one community maintain meaning through use?|Use permission and specify place, period, and practice.
field_regional_variation|Related Places in Two Regions|How do local traditions differ around similar landscapes?|Compare sources and community explanations without ranking authenticity.
field_translation_issue|A Place Name in Translation|How does translation change what a map or story seems to locate?|Compare original terms, geography, and custodial use.
field_intercommunity_contact|A Shared or Contested Place|What records show interaction among communities at one site?|Attribute claims, date arrangements, and include affected voices."""

if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("450", "450_sanskrit_learning", SANSKRIT,
                  "Sanskrit learning pathways, text selection, grammar and translation, teaching methods, assessment, and equitable access.",
                  "dated curricula and textbooks, source editions and dictionaries, assessment data, institutional records, and consented learner and teacher accounts",
                  "State learner level, language register, text edition, and assessment goal. Avoid promising fluency from a short course; distinguish language learning from ritual authority and respect learner privacy.")
    revise_domain("240", "240_sacred_geography", SACRED,
                  "Sacred landscapes as living places shaped by named communities, maps, history, access, ecology, and stewardship.",
                  "dated texts and maps, heritage and land records, environmental assessments, access rules, and consented custodian and resident accounts",
                  "Attribute sacred meanings and disputed place claims; date maps and distinguish official boundaries from lived geography. Respect restricted locations, custodial protocols, and current access rules.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
